                <pb facs="0685" n="583" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.101/8</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Fish</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 108</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-07-12">July 12, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The receipt is acknowleged of your
                    despatch No. 266 of May 23, 1935, transmitting a copy of a note which you
                    addressed to the Egyptian Ministry of Foreign Affairs on May 22, 1935,
                    concerning the recent reorganization of the Municipality of Alexandria. It is
                    observed that in the penultimate paragraph of the note in question you stated
                    that “the Government of the United States therefore considers the unilateral
                    action of the Egyptian Government in reorganizing the Municipality of Alexandria
                    as likely to impair existing capitulatory rights of American interests in
                    Egypt”. Inasmuch as the Department’s instruction No. 84 of April 29, 1935,
                    merely authorized you to enter a reservation of this Government’s position the
                    Department would not wish you to continue to press the view that the
                    reorganization of the Alexandria Municipality is likely to impair existing
                    capitulatory rights of American interests in Egypt.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
